pandoc
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Component:  pandoc
Version:    3.9
Licence:    GPL-2.0-or-later
Upstream:   https://pandoc.org  (source: https://github.com/jgm/pandoc)
Copyright:  Copyright (C) 2006-2024 John MacFarlane

How it reaches a rebar install
    pandoc is NOT vendored in this repository and is not a required dependency.
    The executable is bundled inside the third-party `pypandoc-binary==1.17`
    wheel, which is pulled in ONLY by the optional `wiki` extra
    (`pip install rebar[wiki]`). An install without that extra contains no
    pandoc, and the Data Center wiki renderer degrades to passing Markdown
    through unchanged.

    One DEVELOPER-ONLY path also fetches pandoc. That wheel's arm64 macOS
    payload is an x86_64 executable, so on an arm64 macOS host it cannot run
    (bug bb19-4776-46d2-4223). `make install` therefore runs
    `scripts/ensure_pandoc.py`, which downloads the same pandoc 3.9 recorded
    here from the upstream GitHub release, verifies its SHA-256 against a
    hard-coded pin, and writes it to the git-ignored `.tools/bin/`. Nothing
    there is committed, packaged, or redistributed; it exists only so a
    developer's own checkout can run the renderer tests.

How rebar uses it
    The renderer (src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py)
    locates the bundled binary via pypandoc and executes it as a
    SEPARATE PROCESS, communicating over stdin/stdout. rebar does not link
    against pandoc, does not embed its code, and does not derive from it.

Obligation
    pandoc is GPL-2.0-or-later. Anyone REDISTRIBUTING a bundle that includes the
    pandoc executable — for example a container image or a wheel built with the
    `wiki` extra baked in — carries the GPL's source-availability obligation for
    pandoc itself. Upstream source is at the URL above; the pinned version is the
    one recorded here, and the pin is verified in CI so this entry cannot drift
    from what is actually shipped.
